To determine if a graph contains a cycle, you can use a depth-first search (DFS) traversal of the graph. Starting from any node, follow the edges to visit its neighbors until you reach a previously visited node. If you reach a previously visited node, then there is a cycle in the graph.

Here's a Python implementation:

```python
def detect_cycle(graph):
    visited = set()

    def dfs(node):
        if node in visited:
            return True
        visited.add(node)
        for neighbor in graph[node]:
            if dfs(neighbor):
                return True
        return False
    return any(dfs(node) for node in graph)
```

