You can implement the Gauss-Jordan elimination method to solve the system of linear equations using Python. The Gauss-Jordan elimination method is a well-known algorithm for solving systems of linear equations.

Here is a Python implementation of the Gauss-Jordan elimination method:

```python
def gauss_jordan_elimination(A, b):
    n = len(A)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            if A[i][i] != 0:
                factor = A[j][i] / A[i][i]
                for k in range(i, n):
                    A[j][k] -= factor * A[i][k]
                b[j] -= factor * b[i]
    x = [0] * n
    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):
        x[i] = (b[i] - sum(A[i][j] * x[j] for j in range(i+1, n))) / A[i][i]
    return x
```

