To calculate the Fibonacci sequence using memoization, we can use a dictionary to store previously calculated values. This approach reduces the time complexity from O(2<sup>n</sup>) to O(n) by caching the intermediate results. The memoized function will check if the nth Fibonacci number is already present in the dictionary. If it is, it will return the cached value, otherwise, it will calculate the value and store it in the dictionary before returning it.

```python
def fibonacci_memoized(n):
    memo = {0: 0, 1: 1}
    def _fibonacci(n):
        if n not in memo:
            memo[n] = _fibonacci(n-1) + _fibonacci(n-2)
        return memo[n]

    return _fibonacci(n)
```

